.TH INGOT 1 "2026-09-07" "ingot 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ingot \- Docker-compatible container engine client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ingot
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ingot
is the command-line client for the Ingot container engine. It talks to the
.BR ingotd (1)
daemon over a Unix socket (default
.IR /run/ingot/ingot.sock ).
Per-command help is authoritative:
.B "ingot \fICOMMAND\fR \-\-help"
lists the exact flags.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-host " \fIHOST\fR"
Daemon socket (e.g. \fIunix:///run/ingot/ingot.sock\fR).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B version\fR, \fBping\fR, \fBinfo
Daemon reachability and version information.
.TP
.B run
Run a command in a new container. Supports
.BR \-d ,
.BR \-i ,
.BR \-t ,
.BR \-\-name ,
.BR \-p / \-\-publish ,
.BR \-e / \-\-env ,
.BR \-v / \-\-volume ,
.BR \-\-network ,
.BR \-\-rm ,
.BR \-w / \-\-workdir ,
.BR \-\-dns ", " \-\-dns\-search ", " \-\-dns\-opt ,
.BR \-\-restart ,
.BR \-\-memory ,
.BR \-\-cpus ,
.BR \-\-pids\-limit ,
.BR \-\-cap\-add ", " \-\-cap\-drop ,
.BR \-\-privileged ,
.BR \-\-user .
.TP
.B pull
Pull an image from a registry (digest pinning and platform selection
supported).
.TP
.B login\fR, \fBlogout
Store or remove registry credentials (mode 0600).
.TP
.B ps
List containers:
.BR \-a ,
.BR \-q ,
.BR \-\-no\-trunc ,
.BR \-\-format " table|json" ,
.BR \-f .
.TP
.B images
List images:
.BR \-q ,
.BR \-\-no\-trunc ,
.BR \-\-format " table|json" ,
.BR \-f .
.TP
.B stop\fR, \fBkill\fR, \fBrm
Stop, kill, or remove containers.
.TP
.B logs
Fetch container logs. Supports
.BR \-\-follow " (short " \-f ),
.BR \-\-tail .
.TP
.B exec
Run a command in a running container. Supports
.BR \-i ,
.BR \-t .
.TP
.B rmi\fR, \fBtag\fR, \fBcp
Remove/tag images; copy files between a container and the host.
.TP
.B network
Manage networks (create, inspect, list, remove, connect, disconnect, prune).
.TP
.B volume
Manage volumes (create, inspect, list, remove, prune).
.TP
.B system
Daemon-wide information and space reclamation.
.TP
.B build
Build an image from a Dockerfile:
.BR \-t ,
.BR \-f ,
.BR \-\-no\-cache ,
.BR \-\-no\-cache\-filter ,
.BR \-\-secret ,
.BR \-q .
.TP
.B compose
Docker Compose (up, down, ps, logs). Services support
.B pull_policy
and health/completion-gated
.BR depends_on .
.TP
.B doctor
Check system requirements and engine health (socket, cgroup v2,
overlayfs, iproute2, iptables, seccomp, data paths, schema marker).
.TP
.B completions
Generate shell completions.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/ingot/ingot.sock
Daemon socket. Anyone with access has effective root on the host.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ingot/auth.json
Stored registry credentials (mode 0600).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ingotd (1),
.BR docker (1)
.SH NOTES
Ingot targets the Docker Engine API v1.44 surface documented in
.IR docs/DOCKER_MATRIX.md .
Unsupported options fail with an explicit error instead of being
silently ignored.
